update public.journal_articles set title = 'How NMN works at the cellular level to delay aging', summary = 'Nicotinamide mononucleotide (NMN) has captured the attention of the scientific world. Find out how it restores NAD+ levels and directly influences longevity.', content = 'NAD+ (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide) is an essential coenzyme present in every living cell, responsible for energy production and DNA repair. As we grow older, NAD+ levels fall dramatically, setting off the processes of cellular aging.

NMN is the direct precursor of NAD+. Recent clinical studies show that supplementing with pure, pharmaceutical-grade NMN can raise the body''s NAD+ reserves quickly and efficiently. This reactivates the sirtuins (the so-called "longevity genes"), improves mitochondrial function and protects the integrity of the genome.

At Longevity Pharma we chose a formula with a purity of >99%, because unstable or impure NMN molecules can degrade into plain nicotinamide and lose their anti-aging properties.', author = 'The Longevity Pharma Medical Team', tags = ARRAY['Biohacking', 'Anti-aging', 'NMN']::text[] where id = '52ec529d-9129-40e8-8e8f-114c69c94eb5';
update public.journal_articles set title = 'Hydrolyzed collagen vs. native collagen: what do the clinical studies say?', summary = 'The difference between the types of collagen determines how effective they are. Discover why molecular weight is the single most important factor in absorption.', content = 'The supplement market is flooded with all kinds of collagen formulas, yet few consumers know how much molecular mass matters. Native collagen, excellent though it is in theory, has a molecule too large to cross the intestinal barrier intact.

The enzymatic hydrolysis process used in modern laboratories turns raw collagen into peptides of microscopic size (under 2000 Daltons). This hydrolyzed form of collagen is absorbed into the bloodstream at a rate of over 90%, reaching the fibroblasts that synthesize new connective tissue for the skin, the joints and the blood vessels.

Our recommendation is a hydrolyzed marine collagen from sustainable sources, whose bioavailability exceeds that of bovine or porcine versions.', author = 'The Longevity Pharma Medical Team', tags = ARRAY['Ingredients', 'Nutrition', 'Joints']::text[] where id = '68f70486-ed1b-44ca-bc85-eab54dc0ae9e';
update public.journal_articles set title = 'A complete protocol for reducing inflammation and oxidative stress', summary = 'Chronic low-grade inflammation is the source of most modern conditions. Here is the daily protocol validated by experts for fighting it.', content = 'Silent or chronic inflammation shows no immediate symptoms, yet over time it damages tissue and accelerates cellular senescence. The oxidative stress generated by free radicals is the main engine of this kind of inflammation.

The protocol our experts propose involves a three-step approach:
1. **Neutralizing free radicals:** taking powerful antioxidants such as resveratrol or glutathione, which donate electrons to unstable molecules without becoming harmful themselves.
2. **Modulating the immune response:** optimizing vitamin D3 and zinc levels, both essential for a balanced immune system that does not overreact.
3. **Lowering inflammatory markers:** introducing high-purity omega-3 fatty acids (with an optimal EPA/DHA ratio) to bring down the level of pro-inflammatory cytokines.

Supplementation should be paired with sunlight exposure in the first hours of the morning and at least 7 hours of restorative sleep.', author = 'The Longevity Pharma Medical Team', tags = ARRAY['Protocols', 'Immunity', 'Lifestyle']::text[] where id = '90863fa8-870a-4a6f-a2cd-bfc977154886';
update public.journal_articles set title = 'Why we test every production batch in a third-party laboratory', summary = 'Quality is not declared, it is demonstrated. Find out what independent laboratory testing involves and why it is essential for your safety.', content = 'The food supplement industry is often a gray area when it comes to strict regulation. Many manufacturers rely solely on the certificate of analysis issued by the supplier of the raw material - a practice prone to errors and inaccuracies.

At Longevity Pharma we apply the "Trust, but Verify" standard. Every batch of finished product is sent to an independent laboratory (third-party testing) for analysis. What exactly are we looking for?
- **Identity and potency:** we make sure there really are 500mg of the active substance declared on the label, not 450mg and not a similar chemical compound.
- **Microbiology:** we check for the absence of dangerous bacteria, molds and yeasts.
- **Heavy metals:** we test for lead, mercury, cadmium and arsenic, using extremely strict standards (USP/EP).

Only the products that pass this "gold filter" reach you, guaranteeing you maximum efficacy and zero risk.', author = 'The Longevity Pharma Medical Team', tags = ARRAY['Quality', 'Transparency']::text[] where id = '56260326-36a2-48b4-ab15-b153fcef6011';

